{"title":"2023 IOQM/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IOQM/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A quadruple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8c31b328eb3b0252134a4720e161c0fdf641e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c, d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> of distinct integers is said to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30a94c290b478bf2f822b781fad0833fccaec334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{balanced}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf957053351e009f9d88b947a1951751bfe764d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + c = b + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be any set of quadruples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8c31b328eb3b0252134a4720e161c0fdf641e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c, d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/668506f2a9b7b0d3d8a804ce43b9373ebcfe3257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq a &lt; b &lt; d &lt; c \\leq 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"185\" height=\"17\" /> and where\nthe cardinality of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c66dedcc784161b488431d3025171b13e42a4bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4411$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Find the least number of balanced quadruples in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e070383e926439d2af0a58994af4e2782364c8a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"16\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IOQM/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5ccf63afc440e044173514d3602ada5440f3fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S} \\in \\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the set of all possible quadruples of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8c31b328eb3b0252134a4720e161c0fdf641e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c, d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/668506f2a9b7b0d3d8a804ce43b9373ebcfe3257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq a &lt; b &lt; d &lt; c \\leq 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"185\" height=\"17\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d07416f8fa5aee86d5e863bbde3f368481b4c556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(\\mathcal{T}) = ^{20}C_4 = 4845$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/678982b9843fc0f306028fe8bb7dc0920f140121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(\\mathcal{T} \\cap \\mathcal{S&#39;}) = 4845 - 4411 = 434$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"249\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Now, let us try to find all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f25e90dfb88961a9800d033b0c32c9e5ff95afd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$balanced$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> quadraples in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/3/7a373ca268e571b56cb554f6c36de2561c0b6eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + c = b + d = k = 3,\\ 4,\\ 5,\\ \\dots,\\ 38,\\ 39$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c446bcfac98f31d890a9c810a1556cbf4e20be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq a &lt; c &lt; b &lt; d \\leq 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"185\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>For each value of sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/7986e00dd444fd27c0a2e795fdb31b83202f4dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\leq 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e06dc6b79ca7c9d352c331bf0d75b81821ef090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_k = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{k-1}{2} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"115\" height=\"45\" /> possible unordered ways to distribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> into the sum of two distinct numbers excluding repeats and cases where the numbers are equal.\n</p><p>For each value of sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f042cc2a5d4cc47f8a5c332a5c230e2f8acb0d54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf9b69a72fd021d1212015c45908d3d5bae40cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_k = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{k-1}{2} \\right\\rfloor - (k - 21)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"202\" height=\"45\" /> possible unordered ways to distribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> into the sum of two distinct numbers excluding repeats, cases where the numbers are equal, or invalid cases where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/3758325f04957cde49c7c37aea6466abb67ae5c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,\\ b,\\ c,\\ d &gt; 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e0144cc413455165eb4511d16aeaec58decb30ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_k = 1,\\ 1,\\ 2,\\ 2,\\ 3,\\ ,3\\ ,\\ \\dots,\\ 9,\\ 9,\\ 10,\\ 9,\\ 9,\\ 8,\\ 8,\\ \\dots,\\ 1,\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"474\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since any two unordered sums produce a unique value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/c/44c4d5ab85694272fa9868aad4d4449a5b1b29df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,\\ b,\\ c,\\ d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, the total number of quadruples = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78deaa6b76af6a7b32b7647a2ad163e17b2e05b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^1C_2 + ^1C_2 + ^2C_2 + ^2C_2 + ^3C_2 + ^3C_2 + \\dots + ^9C_2 + ^9C_2 + ^{10}C_2 + ^9C_2 + ^9C_2 + ^8C_2 + ^8C_2 + \\dots + ^2C_2 + ^2C_2 + ^1C_2 + ^1C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"925\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5b405b6edd699d454ea9d41e72fa4535d3da6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 4(^1C_2 + ^2C_2 + ^3C_2 + \\dots + ^9C_2) + ^{10}C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"323\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>By the Hockey Stick Identity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8d6144aba5c7be36c228a501126a8457b259b6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 4(^1C_2 + ^2C_2 + ^3C_2 + \\dots + ^9C_2) + ^{10}C_2 = 4 \\cdot ^{9 + 1}C_{2+1} + ^{10}C_2 = ^{10}C_3 + ^{10}C_2 = 4 \\cdot 120 + 45 = 480 + 45 = 525$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"860\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>By PHP, the minimum number of balanced quadruples in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d217dc66244ca8842c2b3cadb53e487e880db3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$525 - 434 = \\boxed{91}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~biggest_glitter_hater\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065116\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 125/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6831/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37601:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018065116 and revision id 291914. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}